All routes are registered and the code compiles. Here's what was implemented:

**`app/auth.py`** — `require_api_key` now reads the `X-API-Key` header, checks it against `VALID_API_KEYS`, raises `HTTP 401` if missing/invalid, and returns the associated username on success.

**`app/main.py`** — six changes:

| Endpoint | Change |
|---|---|
| `GET /tasks` | Added optional query params `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` (combinable filtering) and `page`/`page_size` (pagination, default 1/20) |
| `POST /tasks` | New — auto-generates ID, requires auth (`Depends(require_api_key)`), validates `project_id` exists (404), returns created task with 201 |
| `PUT /tasks/{task_id}` | New — requires auth, partial update via `TaskUpdate.model_dump(exclude_none=True)`, 404 if not found |
| `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` | New — requires auth, 204 on success, 404 if not found |

Key design decisions:
- **Filtering** chains `if`-guarded list comprehensions so all filter combinations work naturally with no special casing
- **Partial updates** use `model_copy(update=...)` which merges only the non-`None` fields from `TaskUpdate` — any omitted field stays unchanged
- **ID generation** derives the next ID from the existing data (`max + 1`) and increments atomically per-call on a module-level counter
